    {
     "type": "code",
     "head": "Second flavor: slow and fast",
     "say": "A second flavor: a slow pointer and a fast one. Slow w marks where the next kept value goes. The loop is the fast pointer. A new value gets copied to w. One, one, two, two, two, three becomes one, two, three, length three. Unsorted input? Sort first, or use a hash map. Next: Two Sum Two, Three Sum, Container With Most Water.",
     "panels": [
      {
       "file": "sol.cpp",
       "code": "int dedupe(vector<int>& a) {\n    int w = 0;\n    for (int x : a)\n        if (w == 0 || x != a[w - 1]) a[w++] = x;\n    return w;\n}"
      }
     ],
