    {
     "type": "code",
     "head": "Fixed window in code",
     "say": "Same thing in code. Cur is the window sum. Each step adds the element entering on the right. Once i reaches k, subtract the element leaving on the left. From the first full window on, record the best. Best starts at the smallest int, so negative arrays work too. It's one pass. On our array it prints nine.",
     "panels": [
      {
       "file": "sol.cpp",
       "code": "int maxSum(const vector<int>& a, int k) {\n    int cur = 0, best = INT_MIN;\n    for (int i = 0; i < (int)a.size(); i++) {\n        cur += a[i];\n        if (i >= k) cur -= a[i - k];\n        if (i >= k - 1) best = max(best, cur);\n    }\n    return best;\n}"
      }
     ],
     "steps": [
